-- One barrier, one pre-state (spec §10): batched effects swap Gold and Silver. Twin of s10-pre-state.bqn.
-- Both `;`-batched effects read the statement's gathered pre-state, so the pair swaps on-mask; rows 0 and 3 are untouched.
-- The naive-sequential half (silverN reads goldN's write, losing the swap) is a BQN-only counterexample unreachable from ano semantics.
--! registry ../registries/s10-pre-state.reg
--! expect gold = 10 2 3 40
--! expect silver = 1 20 30 4

Trickster , Gold = Silver ; Silver = Gold

-- Not actually bound to anything lol.
-- Nord , Septims = "Draugr Coin" ; "Draugr Coin" ; Septims
